{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Then the two men shall stand.</b> The verse speaks of witnesses, and teaches that there is no testimony by women, and teaches that they must give their testimony standing (Shevuot 30)." "<b>Who have the controversy.</b> These are the litigants." "<b>Before YHWH.</b> Let it be regarded by them as though they stand before the Omnipresent, as it is said (Psalms 82) ״בְּקֶרֶב אֱלֹהִים יִשְׁפֹּט״ (Sanhedrin 6)." "<b>Who shall be in those days.</b> Even if he is the least of his generation like Samuel in his generation — you are obligated to treat him with honor."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:42.619701385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}